      <ArticleTitle>Serum Marker X Predicts Sepsis Mortality in <i>Adults</i>.</ArticleTitle>
      <Abstract>
        <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Early risk stratification in sepsis remains poor.</AbstractText>
        <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">In 1,204 adults, serum marker X above 40 ng/mL was associated with a hazard ratio of 2.1 for 28-day mortality. The association did not hold in patients under 30.</AbstractText>
